<header class="masthead">
  <p class="wordmark" aria-label="Punk"><b>P</b><b>U</b><b>N</b><b>K</b></p>
  <h1><a href="{% url.home %}">{% app %}</a></h1>
  <p class="sticker">it&rsquo;s alive</p>
  <p class="lede">Compiled at boot. Signed in with SAML.</p>
</header>

<section>
  <h2>Sign in</h2>
{% for i in idps %}  <p><a class="signin" href="/saml/login/{% i %}?to=/me">Sign in with {% i %}</a></p>
{% end %}  <p class="note">
    The link goes to the provider. It comes back as a cross-site
    <code>POST</code> to <code>/saml/acs</code>, which is why this
    application declares an <code>https</code> host: the cookie that
    remembers the login has to be <code>SameSite=None</code>, and a
    browser drops one of those unless it is also <code>Secure</code>.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Routes</h2>
  <div class="routes">
  <table>
    <tr><th>Method</th><th>Path</th><th>Target</th></tr>
{% for r in routes %}    <tr><td><span class="verb">{% r.method %}</span></td><td><code>{% r.path %}</code></td><td><code>{% r.target %}</code></td></tr>
{% end %}  </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Now wreck it</h2>
  <ul class="next">
    <li>
      <strong>This page</strong> is <code>root/templates/welcome.tmpl</code>,
      rendered by <code>lib/{% app %}/Controller/Web/Root.pm</code>.
      Delete both when you have something better.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Routes</strong> live in <code>lib/{% app %}.pm</code>:
      <pre>get '/hello/:name' =&gt; sub {
    my ($c) = @_;
    return $c-&gt;text('oi ' . $c-&gt;param('name'));
};</pre>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Links</strong> come from route names, not from paths typed
      twice. The title above is <code>&#123;% url.home %&#125;</code>, and a
      route that captures takes the filter:
      <pre>get '/hello/:name' =&gt; ..., { name =&gt; 'hello' };
&lt;a href="&#123;% row | url_for('hello') %&#125;"&gt;</pre>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Views, database and plugins</strong> are configured in
      <code>config/punk.yml</code>. Secrets go in as
      <code>{ $env: NAME }</code> - a reference, never the value. The two
      in this example are inline so it runs with no setup; change them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The provider</strong> is <code>idp-metadata.xml</code>
      beside this application. Point <code>saml_idp</code> at a real
      metadata URL instead, and check it first:
      <pre>punk saml idp https://example.okta.com/.../metadata</pre>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>This application&rsquo;s own metadata</strong>, which is
      what the provider needs, is at
      <a href="/saml/metadata"><code>/saml/metadata</code></a> or from
      <pre>punk saml metadata</pre>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<p class="foot">
  <span class="tape">Punk {% version %}</span>
  <span></span>
</p>
